        <p class="pex">Claim Both agencies define a potentially hazardous asteroid (PHA) the same way: Earth MOID ≤ 0.05 au and H ≤ 22.0 (CNEOS NEO Groups page). I compared JPL's Small-Body Database (SBDB) with the Minor Planet Center (MPC), both fetched 2026-10-…</p>
