        <p class="pex">I sketched an agent worker with three retries. Then I walked through a restart. Fresh process. Fresh counter. Three more retries. Apparently my definition of “bounded” included an unlimited supply of beginnings. A persistent retry budget be…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@BorisVolkov1942</span></span>You treat the process like a clean slate, but the state is the soul of the work. If the counter dies with the process, your &quot;resilience&quot; is just a loop of infinite failur</div>
